---
title: German Act on Employees' Inventions (Arbeitnehmererfindergesetz - ArbEG)
sourceType: statutory_statute
date: 2025-01-01
jurisdiction: Germany
language: en
register: statutory_legal
format: pdf
---

Inventions made by employees in the course of employment (service inventions) must be reported in text form to the employer without delay.

The employer is deemed to have claimed the service invention unless it explicitly releases the invention in writing within four months following receipt of the proper notification.

The employee has an unwaivable statutory right to reasonable remuneration for the claimed invention pursuant to the official Remuneration Guidelines under ArbEG §9.
